UNIT review_summary
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@9b9e5d24ca9d cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs summary({ units, stops }) — the per-contract report written to the
  GitHub job summary; reproduce it exactly, including its code-span cells (R4) and its fail-closed status (R2)
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG review_summary(units: list[record[unit: text, status: text, change: text, tests: text, bindings: text, citations: text]], stops: i64) -> text
ENVELOPE units is a list (empty included) of report rows, each holding the six text fields of the SIG; any further field a
  row carries is never read. Every text is well-formed (any Unicode scalar values, line breaks, Markdown and HTML
  characters included). stops is any i64 (the review only produces counts from 0 up; a negative count is in scope and R5
  says what it renders). Nothing in the envelope throws. Values outside the SIG (a units that is not a list, a row that
  is not a map, a missing or non-text field, a stops that is not an integer) are OUT-OF-DOMAIN below; the js language
  file widens to them.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Render the review's per-contract report as Markdown: a level-2 heading carrying the pass/fail count, a
  six-column table with one row per contract in input order (a status icon, then the unit, change, tests, bindings and
  citations cells), and, when there are Stops, a line counting them. The row values come from the review and can carry
  contract text (unit names, labels), so every non-empty cell is a Markdown code span (R4): nothing inside one renders
  (no emphasis, link, image, autolink or HTML), and its vertical lines are escaped because a GitHub-flavored table splits
  its cells before it reads code spans. The result is one text; every line break is a single LF.
BEHAVIOR
R1 An empty units list yields EMPTY_REPORT (PINNED) followed by the STOPS block of R5 (which is empty unless stops is at
  least 1).
R2 A row PASSES exactly when its status equals the text "pass" (exact comparison: case-sensitive, no trimming). Every
  other status, the empty text and "fail" included, FAILS. F = the number of failing rows, N = the number of rows.
  CITED FIDELITY package — the status fails closed: "PASS", "pass " and "error" all count as failing
R3 For N at least 1 the heading is "## SIR review: " followed by the VERDICT of TABLE VERDICT. NOUN is "contract" when N
  is 1 and "contracts" otherwise; it follows N in both rows (so "1 of 2 contracts failing", "1 of 1 contract failing").
R4 Each row, in input order, renders as ROW (PINNED): the icon is FAIL_ICON for a failing row and PASS_ICON for a passing
  one (R2); each of the five cells is CELL(field), defined in four steps.
  (a) T = the field's text scanned left to right with each match of TABLE CELL_ESCAPE replaced; a CR immediately followed
  by an LF is one match (one space), any other CR or LF is a match on its own; every other character is kept.
  (b) An empty T is the empty cell (CELL is the empty text).
  (c) K = the length of the longest run of consecutive backticks (U+0060) in T, 0 when there is none; FENCE = K + 1
  backticks.
  (d) PAD = one space (U+0020) when T begins with a backtick, or ends with a backtick, or begins with a space and ends with
  a space and holds at least one character outside TRIM_SPACE (PINNED); otherwise PAD is empty.
  CELL = FENCE PAD T PAD FENCE. No other character is altered or escaped.
  CITED FIDELITY package — the fence rule is CommonMark's; the all-space test is the host's trim set, not CommonMark's
R5 The STOPS block is chosen by TABLE STOPS_LINE. A count renders as its decimal digits, no grouping, no plus sign, no
  exponent, at any magnitude of the i64 range. A zero or negative count yields no block.
R6 For N at least 1 the result is REPORT (PINNED): the heading, a blank line, the two fixed table lines, the rows joined by
  single LFs, a final LF, then the STOPS block when there is one (a blank line, the stops line, and a final LF).
TABLE VERDICT — F, N -> the heading's verdict (R3)
  F at least 1 -> FAIL_ICON " " F " of " N " " NOUN " failing"
  F is 0       -> PASS_ICON " " N " " NOUN " passing"
TABLE STOPS_LINE — stops -> the STOPS block (R1, R5)
  stops at most 0  -> no block (the empty text)
  stops is 1       -> LF stops " Stop" STOPS_TAIL LF
  stops at least 2 -> LF stops " Stops" STOPS_TAIL LF
TABLE CELL_ESCAPE — character of a field -> its text in T (R4a)
  CR LF (U+000D U+000A, as a pair)  -> " " (one space)
  CR (U+000D) alone                 -> " "
  LF (U+000A)                       -> " "
  LINE SEPARATOR (U+2028)           -> " "
  PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR (U+2029)      -> " "
  "|" (U+007C)                      -> "\|" (a backslash, then the vertical line)
PINNED text EMPTY_REPORT = "## SIR review" LF "No SIR contract changed." LF CITED R1 — the empty-units text; LF = U+000A
PINNED text PASS_ICON = U+2705 CITED R2 R4 — WHITE HEAVY CHECK MARK, one code point, no variation selector
PINNED text FAIL_ICON = U+274C CITED R2 R4 — CROSS MARK, one code point, no variation selector
PINNED text STOPS_TAIL = ": each one is an annotation on its line, explained in full in the review." CITED R5
PINNED charset TRIM_SPACE = { U+0009, U+000A, U+000B, U+000C, U+000D, U+0020, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000..U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000, U+FEFF } CITED R4d — the ECMAScript WhiteSpace and LineTerminator set the package's all-space test trims; NEXT LINE (U+0085) and MONGOLIAN VOWEL SEPARATOR (U+180E) are NOT in it
PINNED grammar ROW = "| " ICON " | " CELL(unit) " | " CELL(change) " | " CELL(tests) " | " CELL(bindings) " | " CELL(citations) " |" CITED R4 — every separator is exactly one space, a vertical line, one space, also around an empty cell; the line opens with "| " and closes with " |"
PINNED grammar REPORT = HEADING LF LF "| | unit | change | tests | bindings | citations |" LF "|---|---|---|---|---|---|" LF ROW ( LF ROW )* LF STOPS CITED R6 — HEADING per R3, ROW per R4, STOPS per R5 (empty, or LF line LF); the header's first cell is a single space between two vertical lines, the rule line has six cells of three hyphens
INVARIANT the result contains no CR, no LINE SEPARATOR and no PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR. It holds exactly 2 LFs for no rows and
  N + 4 for N rows, plus 2 with a STOPS block. Every row line has exactly seven vertical lines not preceded by a
  backslash (six cells), and every non-empty value cell is one code span whose fence is longer than any backtick run
  inside it, so no value text stands outside a code span.
INVARIANT the heading's verdict and the STOPS block are computed independently: a report may say every contract passes
  and still carry Stops, or fail contracts with no Stops (the two counts are never cross-checked).
OUT-OF-DOMAIN js only, recorded in the js extension oracle: (1) units with no length member (a map) is taken as empty and
  yields EMPTY_REPORT plus the STOPS block; (2) units absent (none) throws; (3) a row that is none throws; (4) a field
  that is missing or none is the empty text before CELL; any other non-text field is the host's text of it ("true",
  "false", "0", "7", "2.5", a list as its elements' texts joined by ",", a map as "[object Object]"), then CELL; a
  missing, none or non-text status fails (R2); (5) a stops that is none, false, the empty text or a text the host reads
  as at most 0 yields no block; any other stops value yields the block when the host's loose comparison stops > 0
  holds, takes the singular only when stops is the number 1 exactly (the text "1" takes "Stops"), and renders as the
  host's text of it ("1.5 Stops", "0.5 Stops", "true Stops").
NOTE rust is omitted. Cause: domain — the review system ships as JavaScript (rdv review and the rederive/sir-review GitHub
  Action); there is no Rust consumer.
ORACLE value -> oracles/review_summary.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 2063650031bff66d8e01c0f02bd525c584b6581d5eca8a8504761ade031a7333
SCOPE IN: R1-R6 over the SIG. OUT: review() that builds the rows and the stops count, the comment body, the annotations
  and the Action's I/O (writing GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY); the js widening's values are OUT-OF-DOMAIN, graded by js only.
